# .loom/resync-ignore -- paths Loom must not overwrite or delete.
#
# One `.loom/`-relative path per line. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored;
# matching is exact (no globs). See `.loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md`.
#
# A pin here is this repo declaring "this path is mine, not Loom's". It also
# turns off the `loom:installed-file-write` PreToolUse guard for that one path
# (#7995), which is what lets an agent create/maintain the file at all.

# Repo-owned guard regression tests (issue #87).
#
# Upstream Loom does not ship this file; it is this repo's own regression test
# for a false DENY in the vendored `loom:installed-file-write` guard
# (`.loom/scripts/lib/installed-file-guard.sh`). Pinned so a `loom update`
# `--clean` sweep cannot delete it, and so a Builder can write it without the
# installed-file-write guard denying its own test.
#
# NOTE: this pin covers the TEST ONLY. The guard bug the test documents is
# deliberately NOT fixed by hand-editing the vendored guard library here -- the
# durable fix belongs upstream and is filed as rjwalters/loom#9154 against
# `defaults/scripts/lib/installed-file-guard.sh` +
# `defaults/hooks/guard-loom-workflow.sh`. Do NOT pin those two paths: a pin
# cannot protect a file Loom *does* ship from an `install.sh
# --confirm-reinstall` re-copy, and it would block every future upstream guard
# fix from reaching this repo.
hooks/tests/test-guard-installed-file-write-cd-relative.sh
